caption: Priests of Niktul
setting-component: priests-of-niktul

The priesthood is the formal interface between France and Niktul. In addition to ordinary divine functions under Godmath, priests have several special roles under the Blood Covenant:

- Sanctifying sacrificial weapons for the monthly Hunt.

- Sanctifying their own weapons without relying on another priest.

- Eventually creating permanently sanctified weapons.

- Praying to Niktul for guidance concerning the night’s required sacrifice count and the remaining quota.

- Interpreting Niktul’s tastes, judgments, and disputed cases concerning valid sacrifice.

This makes the priesthood both religiously and politically important. France cannot reliably maintain the Covenant without enough priests to sanctify weapons, communicate the quota, and interpret the terms of the Hunt.
